title: 'pallet-nfts, pallet-uniques: enforce full deposit transfer on collection owner change'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Aligns `pallet-nfts` and `pallet-uniques` with `pallet-assets` (#12366).

    Changing a collection's owner moves its deposit with `repatriate_reserved`, which is
    best-effort. Under `Polite` fortitude, a lock or freeze on the current owner that overlaps
    their free balance can leave part of the reserved deposit behind. The remainder was
    discarded, so the collection's recorded deposit could end up out of sync with what is
    actually reserved on the new owner.

    The affected calls now reject the dispatch with a new `IncompleteDepositTransfer` error when
    the remainder is non-zero, and the storage layer rolls back the partial move:
    - `pallet-nfts`: `transfer_ownership` and `force_collection_owner`.
    - `pallet-uniques`: `transfer_ownership`.

    To recover, the current owner must clear or reduce the offending locks or freezes and retry.
crates:
- name: pallet-nfts
  bump: minor
- name: pallet-uniques
  bump: minor
